opus: arm: vcvtaq_s32_f32 is an AArch64-only intrinsic

vroundf() takes the vcvtaq_s32_f32() path whenever __ARM_ARCH >= 8,
but GCC only provides that intrinsic for AArch64 - it does not appear
in arm_neon.h for 32-bit ARM at any -march. Building for armv8-a in
AArch32 therefore fails:

  celt/arm/mathops_arm.h:41:12: error: implicit declaration of
      function 'vcvtaq_s32_f32'; did you mean 'vcvtq_s32_f32'?

Guard it on __aarch64__ only, matching vminvf() and vmaxvf() in the
same header, so 32-bit ARM uses the portable NEON fallback that is
already there.
---
--- a/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h	2026-09-10 00:26:39.297399397 +0800
+++ b/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h	2026-09-10 00:26:39.301399396 +0800
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 
 static inline int32x4_t vroundf(float32x4_t x)
 {
-#  if defined(__aarch64__) || (defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH >= 8)
+#  if defined(__aarch64__)
     return vcvtaq_s32_f32(x);
 #  else
     uint32x4_t sign = vandq_u32(vreinterpretq_u32_f32(x), vdupq_n_u32(0x80000000));
